# Skill: Clean User-Facing Text

Purpose:
  Text hygiene skill: audit suspicious invisible Unicode and clean
  natural-language prose while preserving facts, meaning, and the
  writer's voice. Covers articles, manuscripts, reports, documentation,
  emails, product copy, UI text, Markdown, HTML prose.

Owns: ./

Source: https://github.com/guillaumemeyer/watermarks-remover
Origin: tmp/watermarks-remover/skills/clean-user-facing-text/
Imported: 2026-09-06
Format: anthropic-skill (adapted to .sdd)
License: MIT
Runtime: python3 (scripts run in Docker only — .sdd rule [R59])
Provenance: Layer A allowed, Layer B gated (see watermark-notes.md)

ReadOrder:
   1  @INDEX.sdd
   2  @SKILL.md
   3  @references/detectors.md
   4  @references/writing-in-your-voice.md

Modes:
  APPLY    — clean and finalize owned user-facing text
  AUDIT    — detect-only pass (lists flagged spans, no rewrite)
  REVIEW   — audit a document's text hygiene without changing it

Rules:
  [CUFT1] Unicode cleanup is deterministic; statistical watermark reduction is best-effort.
  [CUFT2] Claims, facts, numbers, names, citations MUST be preserved — never invented.
  [CUFT3] Code, commands, identifiers, paths, APIs, formulas, citations MUST be unchanged.
  [CUFT4] Scripts MUST run inside Docker — no host-level Python execution ([R59]-[R66]).
  [CUFT5] Use only for text the user owns or is authorized to process.

Entry:
  Read:
    INDEX.sdd
    SKILL.md

  Resolve:
    references/detectors.md
    references/responsible-use.md
    references/watermark-notes.md
    references/writing-in-your-voice.md
    scripts/ (Docker-gated)

Navigation:
  CleanUserFacingText: @INDEX.sdd
  Skill: @SKILL.md
  Detectors: @references/detectors.md
  VoiceGuide: @references/writing-in-your-voice.md

State: +
